--- body ---

## Context

Observed on PR #1178 (wave A, 2026-10-03): rename-aware stat = 14 files,
`--no-renames` roster = 15 — the breaker boundary. Observed again on
PR #1179 (wave B, the 1018 consolidation): gate-rule count 26
(`--no-renames`), `--name-status -M` 19 entries, content-bearing ~15 —
every `git mv` registers as delete+add and pure renames (R100) inflate a
consolidation diff past the 15-file breaker without adding any review
load. The breaker fired on rename arithmetic, not on review substance.

## Actions

1. In skills/gaze/SKILL.md Phase 1 (PR size computation): compute
   `pr_files` from the rename-aware diff, counting CONTENT-BEARING
   entries only: Added, Modified, Deleted, and Renamed-with-edit
   (similarity < 100) each count 1; a pure rename (R100, zero line
   change) counts 0. `pr_lines` stays total insertions + deletions
   (rename-aware — pure renames contribute nothing). State the rule in
   one sentence next to the computation.
2. Same counting in the verdict-time re-check the gate runs (the
   0990-landed sentence): the re-check counts content-bearing files.
3. Keep the threshold itself untouched: `>= 15` content-bearing files
   still fires `circuit_breaker: un-reviewable`. The borrowed threshold
   (rules/workflow.md § Ticket discipline) is unchanged; the refinement
   is gaze's own counting rule for rename-heavy diffs. Do NOT fit the
   threshold to any one PR.
4. The review-pr panel width gate is OUT OF SCOPE (different axis,
   fail-safe direction: --no-renames there can only widen a panel).

## Test

A synthetic diff where 16 entries include 10 pure renames (R100) and 6
content-bearing files must NOT fire the breaker; 16 content-bearing
files must fire. Red first against the current --no-renames counting.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] The Phase 1 computation and the verdict-time re-check both count
      content-bearing files, with the rule stated in the skill text
- [ ] The test proves both directions (rename-inflated passes,
      genuinely-large fires)
- [ ] make check passes

## Invariants

- The 15 threshold is not raised or lowered.
- The breaker still pre-empts the battery before any seat fires.
